  "method": "Read-only source review. Literal immonium and activation mass tables are copied from the pinned class test. Internal interval counts and masses are independently derived from source loop conditions, source residue formulas and elemental mass literals. The float-helper oracle independently computes AG b1/b2/y1/y2 for charges 1 and 2, converts results to f32 and sorts with preexisting values. Expected values are not generated by the Rust implementation. No C++ build, execution or live differential comparison.",
  "reference_test": "tests/theoretical_extension_reference.rs",
  "source_test_coverage_limits": "Upstream internal-fragment tests assert short-input termination and increased output for PEPTIDEK, but do not provide a numeric mass table. The ECD source table lists only the first 11 of 17 peaks. The raw m/z helper is exercised through PrecursorPurity self-consistency, not an upstream standalone literal table.",
  "numeric_assertions": {
    "internal_analytical_absolute_tolerance": 1e-09,
    "immonium": "Exact binary64 equality with source decimal literals",
    "CID": "Absolute tolerance 0.0001 for source four-decimal values",
    "ECD": "Absolute tolerance 0.000001 for source seven-decimal values",
    "float_helper": "Exact binary32 equality with independently calculated and rounded values; not captured C++ output"
  },
